  "rationale": "The recording-specific player page (provider-player) titles recording 56029 'Citizen Advisory Committee - Addison, TX' for Jun 01, 2007, with a topic-segmented video index (Recreation and Community Facilities, Education, Business Development, etc.). The June 2007 Council document (citizen-council-june2007) corroborates that a standing Addison Citizen Advisory Committee exists and transmits recommendations to the City Council (Item #S6, 'Process for Receiving the Citizen Advisory Committee Recommendations'), so the title names a real convening body, not merely a program label. That document is a reference to another body and does not make this recording a City Council meeting; no Council participants are proven for this recording, so no joint-meeting membership is asserted. No supplied feed matches the convened body: city-council, bond-committees, community-partnership-committee, comprehensive-plan-advisory-committee, planning-and-zoning-commission, board-of-zoning-adjustment, unified-development-code-advisory-committee, tif, and public-briefings each cover different bodies or event types. The town-meetings feed is a grouping for town halls, open houses and historical citizen input; a convened advisory committee meeting does not fit it under the identity rule (use the convened body, not topic). Per the sparse rule, a real body without an existing dedicated feed is unconfigured, not non-city: return unconfigured_body with no feed slug invented."
